WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you, Kristen?
-Hi, Seth.

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
Great to see you.
I'm doing great.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:05.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm trying to get a few Z'
before tomorrow night.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's gonna be a marathon,
I'm anticipating.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.043 size:88% position:44%
It's great to see you.
-I think a lot of people

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
are worried about insanity
in the coming days,

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, also, a lot of people
feel gratitude

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:18.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
towards you for the sanity
you brought to the proceedings

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the second
presidential debate.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
You even got positive feedback
from President Trump.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:26.259
What was it like hearing tha
he thought you did a good job?

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.763
-Well, first of all, thank you
so much for your nice comments

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was nice that people
on both sides of the aisle

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.301 line:92%
felt as though it had gone well.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.871 size:81% position:41%
My goal, really, Seth,
was just to make sure

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.539 line:92%
that it was a good discussion.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:42.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
To prepare, I reached out to
voters, undecided voters,

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
Democrats, Republicans,
Independents,

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:49.382
and so I got a sense of what
voters wanted to hear about,

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
everything from healthcare
to the economy.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I really tried
to bring that to the debate.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:57.590
And I was really relieved
that people felt as though

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was a good discussion.
That was my goal.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I had doubts about the mute
button being effective...

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-...but it seems, though,

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:07.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
even the threat of one
had an impact.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we did get to hear
both candidates talk more.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know prep is a key
to any debate moderation.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:18.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
What did you plan for
in the days leading up for it?

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:21.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we literally planne
for every scenario.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:25.452
And in order to prepare, I mean,
I spent hours every single day

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:29.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
from like 6:00 a.m.
in the morning until midnigh

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
thinking about
every single question,

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.726 line:92%
crafting every single question

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:36.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
But part of the prep
was just mental preparation,

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:41.901
so I have to give props to m
husband and also to Cody Rigsby,

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
my Peloton instructor,
because I worked out with him,

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, every day
to relieve stress.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:48.908 line:92%
And he's this great motivator.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:52.345
And he would say things like
"I know you're feeling stressed.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know everyone's
going through a lot,"

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:57.117
and I wanted to just say,
"Cody, you have no idea

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.184 line:92%
what I am preparing for."

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:02.255
So, that's how I got prepare
and got through those days

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:02.989 line:92%
leading up to the debate.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.458
-I can only imagine there'
a great deal of preparatio

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.192 size:81% position:41% line:92%
for tomorrow, as well.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
One thing that everyone
seems to be preparing for is

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
one, not knowing
an outcome tomorrow,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:16.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, two, the very real
possibility that the President

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.904 line:92%
will announce an outcome.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:21.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are news anchors,
news reporters,

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
bracing for
these two likelihoods?

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:27.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're gonna be prepared
for any and all possibility,

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:30.984
just like any breaking-new
event that we would be covering.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:34.287
And, really, Seth, it's just
about giving people the facts,

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
making sure that we are
covering things in real time

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.860
as they happen, and making sur
that we're getting it right.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.397
That's the most important part
I think of being a journalist.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.866 size:88% position:44%
And so that's what we're
going to endeavor to do

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:49.669
throughout the day tomorro
as we cover what's gonna b

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.005 line:92%
a really historic election here.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.741
-You got sort of as high
a praise as you could get.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:58.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were played
by Maya Rudolph on "SNL."

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:00.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
You must have known
to some degree that was coming

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:04.350
What was it like seeing yourself
portrayed on "SNL"?

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have to say,
I was almost as anxious

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
thinking about
being portrayed on "SNL"

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.390 line:92%
as I was about doing the debate.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:14.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what an honor to be
portrayed by Maya Rudolph!

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.129 line:92%
She is one of my favorites

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:19.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am just in awe of her
as an actress, as a comedian

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:22.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was literally -- had my face
pressed against the TV

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:26.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
like that, laughing,
and just sort of screaming

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.607 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It was a little surreal.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought
she did a great job.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was so much fun.
I was glad that there was

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:33.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of focus
on the candidates, as well

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.581 line:92%
I do have to say, though, Seth

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the record,
I'm not really a shot girl

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't do shots.
That was a part of the skit.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:42.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm more of a sauvignon blan
kind of a girl.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it was a lot of fun.
-Alright, that is good to know

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
As far as what "SNL"
could get wrong about you,

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.595 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it's not the worst.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:50.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Exactly.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was so much fun.
-You avoided not only

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:58.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
a disaster at the debate,
but you also avoided a disaste

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:03.543
a while back while you were with
Andrea Mitchell, your colleague.

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can we take a look
at this clip real quick?

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:09.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it is quite remarkable
It's not exactly clear.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:10.483 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Politics -- Ooh!

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a little windy
out here, Andrea.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:19.459
-I mean, really good maintaining
of the composure there, Kristen.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.293 line:92%
-You know, I didn't have -

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:23.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
know that I had those reflexes
until that happened.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.331 line:92%
To be totally truthful, though

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:28.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seth, it looked
a lot scarier on TV.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:31.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Andrea, who I refer to
as my D.C. Mom,

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
had this reaction
of just sheer terror.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.443 size:84% position:42%
You can hear her gasp
when those light stands

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:40.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
started falling in front of me
and my mom said,

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.482 size:81% position:41%
"You know, I'm so glad
she reacted that way,

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:43.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that's how
I was reacting

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:45.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I was watching
on my living-room couch."

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:49.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I think she sort of brought
what a lot of moms

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.723 line:92%
were feeling in that moment.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.092
It was lot of fun, though,
and I had some fun with it

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
I started tweeting
at the Eagles --

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:56.095 line:92%
of course, my hometown team.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.531 size:81% position:41%
I'm from Philadelphia,
and saying, you know,

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.632 line:92%
I was ready for the draft pick

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was going on
at that time, so...

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was very nice
that the Eagles noticed.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as a fellow football fan
I can only tell you,

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
when your football team
knows you exist,

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's no higher praise.
-Yeah.

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:13.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was definitely
a great, great day.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, in fact,
I'm in Philly right now, Seth,

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
to cover the election
and all of

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:20.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
the last-minute campaign stops
that are going on.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:24.991
And so, really excited about
the Eagles win this weekend.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hopefully it'll put everybody
in a good mood

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
and get them out
to the polls tomorrow.

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have a great day tomorrow.
-Thank you, Seth.

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really nice talking to you,
Kristen.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.267
-Thanks for having me on.
I really appreciate it.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.702 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So much fun.

